**Findings**
- [Major] Signal forwarding is lossy and tree termination is not verified — `forward` discards whether the wrapper received SIGINT or SIGTERM, while `killProcessByChildProcess(child, false)` always sends SIGTERM on POSIX. It also discards the returned promise/boolean, so the wrapper can write a terminal job state even if descendants are still shutting down or tree-kill fails. Ctrl-C-specific cleanup handlers never run, and the observed exit changes from 130 to 143. Evidence: `cli/src/modules/sessionJob/runSessionJob.ts:167`

